{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 59","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_59&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be relatively prime positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f81051763302a8608017e601613ddfd56bf12a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac ab=\\dfrac1{2^1}+\\dfrac2{3^2}+\\dfrac3{2^3}+\\dfrac4{3^4}+\\dfrac5{2^5}+\\dfrac6{3^6}+\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"314\" height=\"37\" />, where the numerators always increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the denominators alternate between powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, with exponents also increasing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for each subsequent term. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_59&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum can be split into two groups of numbers that we want to add: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fedf0050fdec4a5fa086248f95c77b231b5cb6e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 + \\tfrac{3}{2^3} + \\tfrac{5}{2^5} \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb0cd87b038d743abf756714ff5fead6f5e7876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{2}{3^2} + \\tfrac{4}{3^4} + \\tfrac{6}{3^6} \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the first sequence, so we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3adfc8b1359b82e15475a15cc1f608923e8be2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} X &amp;= \\frac12 + \\frac{3}{2^3} + \\frac{5}{2^5} \\cdots \\\\ \\frac{X}{4} &amp;= 0 + \\frac{1}{2^3} + \\frac{3}{2^5} \\cdots \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}X &amp;= \\frac12 + \\frac{2}{2^3} + \\frac{2}{2^5} \\cdots \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}X &amp;= \\frac12 + \\frac{\\tfrac14}{\\tfrac34} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}X &amp;= \\frac56 \\\\ X &amp;= \\frac{10}{9} \\end{align*}\" width=\"173\" height=\"264\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of the second sequence, so we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f00bd0d6548eb88f4acd3721e1e3fd7d97d74e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Y &amp;= \\frac{2}{3^2} + \\frac{4}{3^4} + \\frac{6}{3^6} \\cdots \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}Y &amp;= 0 + \\frac{2}{3^4} + \\frac{4}{3^6} \\cdots \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}Y &amp;= \\frac{2}{3^2} + \\frac{2}{3^4} + \\frac{2}{3^6} \\cdots \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}Y &amp;= \\frac{\\frac29}{\\frac89} \\\\ Y &amp;= \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac98 \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{9}{32} \\end{align*}\" width=\"178\" height=\"263\" />\nThat means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076993d377424f838bc089c136f94bcf87fe0ee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{a}{b} = \\tfrac{10}{9} + \\tfrac{9}{32} = \\tfrac{401}{288},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/4265efae349f923cf8aa0d7a2bfe500e03f46265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = \\boxed{689}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_59&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a hr